@startuml llm_module
title LLM module -- generic facade + strategy + allocation client (planned)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype polyline

legend top right
  | <#fef3c7> | EXISTING (unchanged) |
  | <#bbf7d0> | PLANNED -- new file/class |
  | <#bfdbfe> | PLANNED -- modified |
  | <#fecaca> | External (Anthropic / OpenAI SDKs) |
endlegend

' ===========================================================
' MODULE: serverV2/llm  -- generic, provider-agnostic
' ===========================================================
package "serverV2/llm" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {

  package "(value objects -- generic chat shape)" <<Rectangle>> #bbf7d0 {
    class LLMChatRequest <<new>> {
      + model : str
      + system : str | None
      + messages : list[dict]   << role + content >>
      + tools : list[dict] | None
      + tool_choice : dict | None
      + max_tokens : int
      + temperature : float | None
    }

    class LLMChatResponse <<new>> {
      + content_blocks : list[dict]   << text / tool_use >>
      + stop_reason : str
      + input_tokens : int
      + output_tokens : int
      --
      + tool_use(name : str) : dict | None
      + text() : str
    }

    class LLMException <<new>> {
      Provider-agnostic error type.
      Wraps timeouts, rate limits, bad responses,
      auth failures.  Each provider maps its SDK
      errors into this so callers only catch one type.
    }
  }

  package "(strategy -- one impl per provider)" <<Rectangle>> #bbf7d0 {
    interface LLMProvider <<Protocol>> {
      + name : str
      + chat(request : LLMChatRequest) : LLMChatResponse
        ' raises LLMException on any failure
    }

    class AnthropicProvider {
      - client : anthropic.Anthropic
      --
      + name : str = "anthropic"
      + chat(request) : LLMChatResponse
        ' resp = client.messages.create(...)
        ' return LLMChatResponse.from_anthropic(resp)
    }

    class OpenAIProvider {
      - client : openai.OpenAI
      --
      + name : str = "openai"
      + chat(request) : LLMChatResponse
        ' resp = client.chat.completions.create(...)
        '    (tool-use shape translated from
        '     Anthropic-style to OpenAI-style here)
        ' return LLMChatResponse.from_openai(resp)
    }

    LLMProvider <|.. AnthropicProvider
    LLMProvider <|.. OpenAIProvider
  }

  package "(registry + facade -- module surface)" <<Rectangle>> #bbf7d0 {
    class LLMProviderRegistry <<new>> {
      - providers : dict[str, LLMProvider]
      --
      + register(provider : LLMProvider)
      + get(name : str) : LLMProvider
        ' raises LLMException("unknown provider")
        ' if name not registered.
      + names() : list[str]
    }

    class LLMFacade <<new>> {
      .. single public entry point ..
      Constructor: takes LLMProviderRegistry.
      --
      + chat(provider_name : str,
             request : LLMChatRequest) : LLMChatResponse
        ' provider = registry.get(provider_name)
        ' return provider.chat(request)
      --
      Future surface (planned but NOT in scope here):
        + chat_stream(...)   -- streaming responses
        + count_tokens(...)  -- pre-call sizing
    }
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' MODULE: serverV2/allocation  -- consumer-side client
' ===========================================================
package "serverV2/allocation" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {

  package "(allocation client -- pure pass-through)" <<Rectangle>> #bbf7d0 {
    class AllocationLLMClient <<new>> {
      .. allocation's view into the LLM module ..
      Constructor: takes LLMFacade.
      --
      + chat(provider_name : str,
             request : LLMChatRequest) : LLMChatResponse
        ' Pure pass-through.  Lives in allocation so
        ' the allocation module never imports
        ' ``serverV2/llm/*`` directly -- only the client.
        ' Mirrors the AllocationClient -> AllocationFacade
        ' layering convention already used elsewhere.
    }
  }

  note bottom of AllocationLLMClient
    Future cost-estimator + any other allocation-domain
    LLM caller goes through THIS client.  Keeps the LLM
    module's import surface inside allocation small and
    swappable -- ``AllocationLLMClient`` could become a fake in
    unit tests without touching the cost estimator code.
  end note
}

' ===========================================================
' MODULE: serverV2/bootstrap.py
' ===========================================================
package "serverV2/bootstrap.py" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class "build()" as Bootstrap <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    Boot wiring additions:
      llm_registry = LLMProviderRegistry()
      llm_registry.register(
          AnthropicProvider(
              api_key=os.environ["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"]))
      llm_registry.register(
          OpenAIProvider(
              api_key=os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]))
      llm_facade = LLMFacade(registry=llm_registry)
      llm_client = AllocationLLMClient(facade=llm_facade)

      ' llm_client then gets injected into any
      ' allocation-side consumer (e.g. the planned
      ' LLMCostEstimator) -- separate puml when we
      ' plan that.
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' Externals
' ===========================================================
package "Anthropic SDK" #fecaca {
  class "anthropic.Anthropic" as AnthropicSDK {
    + messages.create(...)
  }
}
package "OpenAI SDK" #fecaca {
  class "openai.OpenAI" as OpenAISDK {
    + chat.completions.create(...)
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' Relationships
' ===========================================================
LLMFacade --> LLMProviderRegistry : reads
LLMFacade ..> LLMProvider : delegates chat()
LLMFacade ..> LLMChatRequest : accepts
LLMFacade ..> LLMChatResponse : returns
LLMProviderRegistry o-- LLMProvider : holds many

AnthropicProvider --> AnthropicSDK : messages.create
OpenAIProvider --> OpenAISDK : chat.completions.create

AllocationLLMClient --> LLMFacade : pass-through

Bootstrap --> LLMProviderRegistry : constructs + registers
Bootstrap --> LLMFacade : constructs
Bootstrap --> AllocationLLMClient : constructs + injects to allocation consumers

' ===========================================================
' Notes
' ===========================================================
note bottom of LLMProvider
  Strategy pattern.  Adding a new model vendor =
  one new file under llm/providers/ + one line in
  bootstrap.  Existing callers never change.
end note

note bottom of LLMChatRequest
  Anthropic's request shape is the canonical superset
  (system + messages + tools + tool_choice + max_tokens).
  OpenAIProvider translates inbound: tool definitions to
  OpenAI's function-calling shape, system prompt to a
  system-role message, etc.  All translation lives in
  the provider impl, never leaks into callers.
end note

note bottom of LLMFacade
  Single seam.  Nothing inside serverV2/llm/ leaks out
  beyond this class.  Callers depend on (LLMFacade,
  LLMChatRequest, LLMChatResponse, LLMException) only.
end note

@enduml
